<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIA PLACES 12.55 BLN LEVS 2-YR,COUPON T-NOTES.</title>
<headline>BULGARIA PLACES 12.55 BLN LEVS 2-YR,COUPON T-NOTES.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry on</p>
<p>Wednesday placed at par value a special issue of two-year,</p>
<p>floater coupon T-notes worth 12.55 billion levs, the Bulgarian</p>
<p>National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The coupon was set at two points over the BNB central</p>
<p>interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now</p>
<p>set at 14.15 percent monthly or 169.80 percent annually.</p>
<p>Coupon payments are due semi-annually and the principal</p>
<p>will be redeemed at maturity, the central bank said in a</p>
<p>statement.</p>
<p>In line with its usual practice the central bank did not</p>
<p>say with which financial intitution or institutions the issue</p>
<p>was placed.</p>
<p>Details of issue follow. Price in percent of par.</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG2030097120</p>
<p> Type			    floater coupon</p>
<p> Term			    two years</p>
<p> Issue date		    April 16</p>
<p> Maturity date		 April 14, 1999</p>
<p> Par value		     12.55 bln levs</p>
<p> Selling price		 100 pct</p>
<p> Yield to maturity	   CIR+2 points</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
